abstract: 'Shi yi xin lu (printed English title: Report of the Peking Hospital), prepared by John Dudgeon and printed at the American Mission Press in Peking in 1870, is held as Bodleian Sinica 1630. This London Missionary Society report discusses the Peking Hospital’s work from 1861 to 1869, charitable care, medical teaching, footbinding and the Chinese circulation of early Western medical knowledge; its closing lists name contributors and record silver amounts. The dataset supports histories of medicine, missions, philanthropy and translation. It provides JSON, TXT and TEI for32content faces in20fixed official captures, a literal table of53source donor entries and parent links for23small notes, with source references and uncertainty records. AI initial transcription, a separately saved reading and nonblind original-image adjudication informed this version. Uncertain readings remain; it has not undergone full human double collation or expert approval.'
